# Regenerable by run.sh — the labeling SURFACE is a pure re-emission of
# the logged flight, and every field it carries is repeated inside
# admission-labels.jsonl (the labeler writes input + verdict per row).
# Committing it would double 2MB of the same bytes.
label-input.jsonl

# A seeded stratified draw from admission-labels.jsonl (see the sampling
# block in the session record) — reproducible, and the 27B's verdicts in
# crosscheck-27b.jsonl carry every input field anyway.
crosscheck-input.jsonl

# Nothing else here is regenerable without a model run: admission-labels.jsonl
# (843 rows, 4B), crosscheck-27b.jsonl (208, 27B), gapquery-arms.json (117
# rewrites, 4B) and gapquery-selfcontainment.json (92 blind 27B verdicts) are
# all measurement OUTPUT and are committed on purpose.
